# Example club admin is public at `/` and `/example`. Do not set these
# Convex / Better Auth keys to run or deploy the public seed club.
# No environment variables are required for `/` or `/example`.
#
# Optional algorithm tunables (same keys as the repo-root .env.example):
# TG_BT_REGULARIZATION=0.1
# TG_BT_MAX_ITERATIONS=500
# TG_BT_TOLERANCE=1e-6
# TG_MIN_COMPARISONS=3
# TG_MIN_OPPONENTS=2
# TG_TOP_K_REFERRALS=5
#
# `/club` only — official Convex + Better Auth (labs.convex.dev/better-auth).
# Unauthenticated /club shows sign-in, never the seed board. Signed-in
# owners get the Convex-backed board only when these are set and
# `npx convex dev` is running in apps/club.
#
# Next.js (.env.local) — generated by `npx convex dev` plus the site URL:
# CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:adjective-animal-123
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=https://adjective-animal-123.convex.cloud
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_SITE_URL=https://adjective-animal-123.convex.site
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
#
# Convex deployment (not Next). Same SITE_URL as NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL:
# npx convex env set BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=$(openssl rand -base64 32)
# npx convex env set SITE_URL http://127.0.0.1:3000
